{"timestamp": 1779394828.019752, "event_type": "phase_changed", "tick": 14, "data": {"phase": "discussion"}}
{"timestamp": 1779394837.78091, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 14, "data": {"player_id": "player_3", "message": "I found Frank\u2019s body in electrical. My route was weapons -> security -> navigation -> back through security -> electrical, and when I entered electrical I saw Frank dead there and reported immediately.\n\nOnly person I saw this round was Eve in navigation around ticks 7-9. I also saw Eve move from security to navigation earlier at tick 4. I didn\u2019t see anyone else near electrical, and nobody was with me when I found the body."}}
{"timestamp": 1779394853.1104698, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 14, "data": {"player_id": "player_0", "message": "I started electrical, then went to medbay, storage, and lower engine. I saw Frank alive in medbay around ticks 2-3. Bob entered medbay from storage at tick 3, and I saw Bob in medbay through tick 5. Frank left medbay toward electrical at tick 4, so that lines up with him ending up dead there.\n\nLater I was in lower engine and saw Charlie there around tick 12; Charlie left lower engine toward storage at tick 13. I didn\u2019t see Diana or Eve at all.\n\nSo the main thing I can add is: Frank was definitely alive in medbay early and went to electrical at tick 4. Bob was the only other person I saw near that side shortly after, but I don\u2019t know where Bob went after medbay. Not hard accusing yet, just Bob\u2019s path after tick 5 matters."}}
{"timestamp": 1779394866.6668968, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 14, "data": {"player_id": "player_1", "message": "Alice has the early game perfectly right. I was in medbay with her and Frank around ticks 3 to 5. After Frank headed off toward electrical and Alice went down to storage, I went north to the cafeteria and then over to upper engine to work on my tasks there. I\u2019ve pretty much just been between upper engine and cafeteria for the rest of the round and haven't seen anyone else since medbay. \n\nI definitely didn't follow Frank into electrical. Since I was north and didn't see anyone pass through cafeteria, the killer must have either stayed south near storage or come from the security/weapons side. Diana mentioned her route on the right side, so I'm very interested to hear where Charlie and Eve were to see if we can narrow down who crossed paths with Frank."}}
{"timestamp": 1779394889.956397, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 14, "data": {"player_id": "player_4", "message": "I started in security, went to navigation, then later went to storage where I was when the meeting got called. I saw Diana enter navigation from security at tick 7, and we were both in navigation around ticks 7-9. I didn\u2019t see Frank, Alice, Bob, or Charlie at all.\n\nDiana\u2019s account of seeing me in navigation matches what I saw, but it also means Diana was definitely on the security/electrical side right before reporting in electrical. Bob is also important here because Alice says Frank left medbay toward electrical at tick 4 and Bob was still nearby through tick 5, so Bob\u2019s path after that matters a lot.\n\nRight now I\u2019d say the main possible suspects from opportunity are Bob or Diana. I don\u2019t have enough to hard accuse yet, but I want to hear Charlie\u2019s route before deciding."}}
{"timestamp": 1779394910.721588, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 14, "data": {"player_id": "player_2", "message": "I started oxygen, went through upper engine, then down to lower engine. I only saw Alice this round \u2014 she came into lower engine from storage around tick 12, and we were both there around tick 13.\n\nOne thing I want to correct: Alice said I left lower engine toward storage at tick 13, but from my side I was still in lower engine with her when the meeting got called. Maybe she mis-saw, but that detail is off.\n\nI did not see Bob at all in upper engine, even though he says he was between upper engine and cafeteria after medbay. Timing could explain it, but his path is totally unconfirmed. With Frank leaving medbay toward electrical at tick 4 and Bob being the last confirmed near him, Bob feels like the strongest suspect to me unless Diana self-reported. Diana and Eve at least match each other in navigation ticks 7-9. So I\u2019m leaning Bob here."}}
{"timestamp": 1779394925.711072, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 14, "data": {"player_id": "player_3", "message": "My info is the same as I reported: I found Frank dead in electrical and hit report immediately. My route was weapons \u2192 security \u2192 navigation \u2192 back through security \u2192 electrical. I saw Eve go security to navigation at tick 4, then I saw Eve in navigation with me around ticks 7-9. I didn\u2019t see anyone else.\n\nAfter hearing everyone, Eve and I do line up on navigation, and Alice/Charlie mostly line up in lower engine late, aside from that small detail about whether Charlie left. The important window seems earlier: Alice saw Frank alive in medbay, Frank went toward electrical at tick 4, and Bob was the last confirmed person near him but then has no confirmation afterward. Charlie also says he never saw Bob in upper engine, which makes Bob\u2019s route weaker.\n\nI know self-report is possible from your perspectives, but from mine Bob has the clearest opportunity and the least confirmed path. I\u2019m leaning Bob unless someone has a stronger reason not to."}}
{"timestamp": 1779394946.196756, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 14, "data": {"player_id": "player_0", "message": "I want to clarify the Charlie detail: from what I saw, Charlie moved out of lower engine toward storage at tick 13. If he says he was still there, maybe it was right as the meeting got called or a timing/vision thing, but that\u2019s what I saw.\n\nFor the kill, I still think the key window is Frank leaving medbay toward electrical at tick 4. Bob was in medbay with us through tick 5, and after that his route is the least confirmed. Charlie says he didn\u2019t see Bob in upper engine, and nobody else can back Bob up after medbay.\n\nDiana self-report is technically possible because she found the body, but Diana and Eve match each other in navigation, and that makes Bob look more suspicious to me. I\u2019m leaning Bob as the best vote."}}
{"timestamp": 1779394972.111528, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 14, "data": {"player_id": "player_1", "message": "Hold on, everyone is tunnel-visioning on me based on Charlie's statement, but let's actually think about the timing for a second. \n\nCharlie, you said you started in Oxygen, went through Upper Engine, and then all the way down to Lower Engine where you met Alice at tick 12. I didn't leave Medbay until tick 5. By the time I walked up through the Cafeteria and finally got to Upper Engine, you were already moving south towards Lower Engine! Of course you didn't see me\u2014we completely missed each other in the rotation. My route is unconfirmed simply because I was in an empty part of the ship after that.\n\nNow, look at Diana's route. She just admitted her path was Weapons -> Security -> Navigation -> Security -> Electrical. Eve can only vouch for her in Navigation around ticks 7-9. That means Diana's return trip from Security to Electrical is completely un-vouched for! She walked straight into Electrical, the exact room Frank went to, and \"found\" the body. \n\nThis is a classic self-report. She killed Frank on her way back up from Navigation because she knew she had no alibi once she separated from Eve, so she hit the button immediately to control the narrative and blame the person last seen with him early on. \n\nPlease don't throw this on a simple timing misunderstanding between me and Charlie. The person who actually went to the body's location and has an unconfirmed window right when the death probably happened is Diana. I'm voting Diana."}}
{"timestamp": 1779394997.152025, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 14, "data": {"player_id": "player_4", "message": "I want to be precise: I can only vouch for Diana being in navigation with me around ticks 7-9. I do **not** clear her after that, because she left back toward security/electrical and I went to storage.\n\nThat said, Bob, the concern isn\u2019t only that Charlie didn\u2019t see you in upper engine. The bigger issue is Frank left medbay toward electrical at tick 4, and you were the last confirmed person near him after that. Your entire route after medbay is unconfirmed, and you could have gone into electrical, killed Frank, and left before Diana arrived much later.\n\nDiana self-report is possible, but for that to be the case she\u2019d have to kill Frank after being with me in navigation, then immediately report in electrical. Bob had the earlier and cleaner opportunity right after Frank went there.\n\nSo I\u2019m still leaning Bob as the stronger vote here."}}
{"timestamp": 1779395020.310598, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 14, "data": {"player_id": "player_2", "message": "I\u2019ve heard Bob\u2019s defense, and the timing explanation for missing me in upper engine is possible, but it still doesn\u2019t actually confirm him. My only confirmed info is still: I went oxygen \u2192 upper engine \u2192 lower engine, and I only saw Alice in lower engine at ticks 12-13. I never saw Bob on my route.\n\nFor me the strongest point is still that Frank left medbay toward electrical at tick 4, and Bob was the last confirmed player near that whole area afterward. Bob\u2019s claimed route after medbay has no witnesses. Diana self-report is possible, but Diana and Eve at least match each other in navigation, and there\u2019s no evidence Frank was alive late enough for Diana to be the more likely killer.\n\nSo unless we\u2019re skipping, I think Bob is the best vote."}}
